From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] light: use the Surface color sensor data type

Surface Pro 11 firmware exposes its usable ambient-light measurement through
Microsoft's composite "color" sensor. The standard "ambient_light" endpoint
is present but reports zero. Both reports use the standard repeated-float
payload, with illuminance in element zero.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/src/libssc-sensor-light.c b/src/libssc-sensor-light.c
index e0bd99a..f399ff7 100644
--- a/src/libssc-sensor-light.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor-light.c
@@ -274,7 +274,7 @@ ssc_sensor_light_new (GCancellable *cancellable, GAsyncReadyCallback callback, g
 			cancellable,
 			callback,
 			user_data,
-			SSC_SENSOR_DATA_TYPE, "ambient_light",
+			SSC_SENSOR_DATA_TYPE, "color",
 			NULL);
 }
 
